      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Second Amendment debate revolves around the interpretation of the amendment, with originalism and living constitutionalism presenting opposing views. Originalists argue that the amendment's text and historical context support a right to bear arms as a collective militia function, whereas living constitutionalists view the amendment as a guarantee of an individual right to bear arms for personal protection. Originalists contend that the Founding Fathers intended the amendment to be applicable in a collective, militia context, while living constitutionalists argue that this interpretation is historically inaccurate and that the Supreme Court's 2008 decision in District of Columbia v. Heller established a clear individual right.",
